## #01 — Notes and the handoff contract
Write06.17.md FIRST, then evidence/handoff05.17/CONTRACT.md, then code. Implement
one standard-library fixture module labs/capture-handoff-pass01/handoff.py with
README, tests and demo. Use the accepted design05.16 plus CH-01/CH-02 from Prime
review. No app/core changes, live jobs, routing, automatic allocation or models.
This is fixture integration, not a new authority or seated workflow.

## #02 — Enforce one explicit binding before capture
Strict versioned input with duplicate-key/type/unknown-field refusal. Explicit
absolute store, instructions_base, book, source_root, handoff record location;
job id, returned event hash, assignee, origin book/page/batch, reserved member and
submission, final report relative path/hash/bytes, artifact source/logical/hash/bytes.
The final report MUST match a returned Clerk artifact path/hash/bytes, as must each
captured artifact. Define source_root versus Clerk artifact-base mapping explicitly;
no guessed relative base or arbitrary byte-identical file from elsewhere. work_ref
is a supplied label, not independently verified job identity. Require usable
instructions and clean returned-state/event/completion/artifact inspection.
Use pinned Clerk f697a7e4..., capture8f3da5c6..., inspector947915fe... (full
manifest hashes); check all before launch, current Python/argument arrays/no shell.
Read status via tool interfaces; do not parse Clerk event internals or recreate
receipt validation. Named reserved member/submission/origin/ordered logical outputs
must match. Delegate path/capture guards to accepted tools; add the adapter's
stricter report-under-source-root requirement. Refuse links and ambiguous mappings.

## #03 — Durable identity, retries and partials
Create an exclusive handoff intent outside the member and Clerk job directory,
before invoking capture, recording a canonical binding hash, exact returned event
and source identities. Define a contained noncolliding record directory; ordinary
Git working trees are allowed for books, not Clerk stores. No control-dir writes.
After fresh verify/inspect and payload comparison, write a completed handoff record
linking binding/event/reservation/manifest/receipt. An identical completed retry
rechecks actual evidence and writes NOTHING. Changed event/report/artifacts/origin/
binding conflicts, even if the capture is complete. An already complete member
without a matching completed handoff record is attention/refusal; do not adopt it.
Incomplete member, interrupted intent, or capture-complete-without-final-record
stays retained and requires attention. No delete, overwrite, automatic resume,
allocation around failure or fabricated success. Failure reporting must state any
actual writes. Pin/source changes between preflight and write must not be claimed
as safe; revalidate bindings and captured payloads, retain conflict evidence. Do not
claim an OS sandbox or immunity to a hostile same-user race.

## #04 — Proof and return
Tests use real pinned tools on disposable stores/books only. Cover clean handoff
with separate transport text, report exact bytes, identical retry tree unchanged,
changed event on complete member, unrelated report, dirty artifacts, claimed job,
unusable instructions, wrong origin/submission/order, preexisting complete without
handoff record, partial member, linked paths and bad pins before any subprocess.
Cover injected failures before/after capture and before final record, plus competing
attempts on the same record: one writer, no overwrite or false successful retry.
Malformed inputs refuse controllably. Private in-process test hooks only, not CLI
fault switches. Record first failures, commands, hashes, skips, actual versus proposed
guards. No new queue/claim/return/reserve during adapter execution; fixture setup
may use them explicitly. Demo shows custody, not review/acceptance/closure.
Run this module's suite, reread notes and disposition them. Do not rerun unrelated
unchanged suites. Only new lab,06.17,evidence/handoff05.17 and named return change.

